\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058  If the string is not wound tight (slack), the initial phase of the draw (x) merely removes the slack without storing energy. The effective power stroke is reduced, leading to negligible exit velocity.

\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 The Operator's Fix:}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058  The SEAL would shorten the string or twist it to induce }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 pre-tension}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 . This ensures that F > 0 (force) from the very first millimetre of the draw, maximising the area under the Force-Draw curve (total work done).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7951058 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 2. External Ballistics: The "Blunt Body" Problem

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 The suction cup arrow represents a unique aerodynamic challenge compared to a standard ogive-tipped projectile.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid7951058\charrsid7951058 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
